{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in","id":42557,"title":"Which Creature/Group would \"Blank\" Fictional Character would be in?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T16:40:29-08:00","id":42557,"title":"Which Creature/Group would \"Blank\" Fictional Character would be in?","content":"i loved the idea that the guys made over the Mage forums, and i thought about keeping with the game but now using ALL world of darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> i always wondered is Ebenizer Scrooge would be a Medium or a Bystander","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:18:34-08:00","id":42665,"title":"","content":"Highschool of the Dead. They're mostly hunters... mostly. For some reason, I want to say that Takashi is a wolf among the sheep, if you will. Or perhaps a tiger or crow. If not, a Judge that managed to get a few Wayward powers.<br /> <br /> Hisashi: Visionary. But not so gifted with foresight, more of the leader type you would expect. Fails to foresee that not carrying a weapon when you are amidst a bunch of zombies and relying on hand to hand combat expertise is a bad idea, but perhaps as one of the Balancers, he might develop Cleave to justify it and last longer?<br /> <br /> Rei: Defender. Fits with her upbringing by a pair of police.<br /> <br /> Saya: Visionary, focuses on long-term planning and foresight. Her parents are Hunter's Hunted-style hunters.<br /> <br /> Kouta: Avenger. Has an Edge that works with guns.<br /> <br /> Saeko: Martyr. Feels that she is just as bad as the monsters she fights.<br /> <br /> Shizuka: Redeemer. She uses Bluster by screaming in a panic.<br /> <br /> Alice: Innocent. Zeke is her familiar, as per the Hermit book.<br /> <br /> Shidou: Wayward. The students left on the bus are his orgiastic cult survivalist followers, but none are more than Bystanders, if that.<br /> <br /> Rika: non-Imbued hunter, along with her spotter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:05:51-08:00","id":42885,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 1987 tv series.<br /> <br /> Eric Cord - Lost Cub<br /> Alamo Joe Rogan - non-Imbued Hunter<br /> Jonas Skorzeny - Black Spiral Dancer<br /> Nicholas Remy - Shadow Lord<br /> Gray Wolf - Bone Gnawer (formerly Red Talon)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:10:05-08:00","id":42957,"title":"","content":"I've recently started watching the anime Ghost Hunt, pretty good series so far. Definitely Orpheus material, minus the actual projection and throw in some more of the psychic powers and Medium aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:28:14-08:00","id":42979,"title":"","content":"ok, to which creed the Winchester boy's (supernatural) belong to, and to which house does Castiel belongs to?.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:39:12-08:00","id":42992,"title":"","content":"Honestly they've been done to death on these forums and I strongly agree with previous comments about them being normal mortal hunters with some knowledge of Sorcery rather than the Imbued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:14:38-08:00","id":43017,"title":"","content":"In that case, the hell is walter white? and would Dexter Morgan be a Wayward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:47:39-08:00","id":43038,"title":"","content":"While a friend of mine and I were reading The Mr. Welsch list and one popped in my head, &quot;If my Malkavian is short, has soul patch and a t-shirt with the words, &quot;Jerk&quot; on it, the ST has the right to kill him off.&quot; In case you don't know, it's the main character from the series, &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Vs.\" target=\"_blank\">Dan Vs</a>&quot;. Of course, he derangement would be paranoia and his cat, Mr. Mumbles&quot;, would be ghouled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:01:31-08:00","id":43077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=43017#post43017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, the hell is walter white? and would Dexter Morgan be a Wayward?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really just start throwing out random fictional characters, there needs to be at least some kind of loose connect between, similar idea/concept between the two universes. You could make Walter White <i>anything</i> in the WoD, a normal mortal criminal to [Insert CWoD Splat Here]. In VtM he could be a Giovanni because of his connections to organized crime or perhaps a Settite because of the drugs he produces. In MtAs he could be a member of the Syndicate or the Cult of Ecstasy for the same reason as well as member of the OoH or the NWO's Ivory Tower because of his academic background. You could also have dying Walter's body possessed by a Fallen or you have him as a wraith after the end of the series. Or you could even radically change things have him instead of turning drug manufacturing get recruited by the Orpheus Group, he wouldn't be the first agent dying of cancer.<br /> <br /> As for Dexter Morgan maybe though if there's one thing he would be in any WoD, he would be a Slasher from the NWoD albeit one who preyed on other Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T23:02:15-08:00","id":43365,"title":"","content":"I've sometimes amused myself with the thought of Angus McGyver being a mage with heavy reliance on props and fate related rotes... Considering his phenomenal success in creating working stuff from almost anything available no matter how ad hoc and they nearly always work just as planned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:24:52-08:00","id":43472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=42979#post42979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, to which creed the Winchester boy's (supernatural) belong to, and to which house does Castiel belongs to?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dean and Bobby non-Imbued (pretty much every Hunter is non-Imbued), Sam is hard. His first Creed would be Avenger (ala Son of Azazael), his second would be a hybrid of Visionary and Hermit (the prophet trials).<br /> <br /> Edit: Dexter would be a Gorehound (CWoD Slasher).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 01-06-2014, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T08:11:14-08:00","id":43529,"title":"","content":"Gorehounds utterly lack the sophistication and capability to operate functionally that Dexter shows, since they keep organs lying around sloppily and, well, just read that letter from the Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition. Not exactly a suave, calculating blood-spatter specialist, there. I think that he'd probably be better utilized as an example of not-nice Ceilican. The Night Priyo even names serial killer as one of the types of people that it encompasses. Alternately, a Hatar. Also makes a convenient way for him to capitalize on exsanguinating his victims. Slurp, slurp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-06-2014, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:56:34-08:00","id":43580,"title":"","content":"I know there was an Al Bundy-eske character in Freak Legions, but I could see him as a Wraith (given all his regrets and such). Peg could also work, but she'd be a Heretic since it would require less work and following the one belief (forgot it's name) based on gambling and luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:56:30-08:00","id":44373,"title":"","content":"Would Nicolas Cage in The Kiss of The Vampire, be a malkavian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:49:29-08:00","id":44450,"title":"","content":"Nicolas Cage <i>is</i> a Malkavian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:56:20-08:00","id":44704,"title":"","content":"During one of the story arc from the comic strip, 9 Chickweed Lane, one of the characters (Seth) was starting to look like prime material for some Nosferatu make into her personal Cleopatra. Seth is a hunky, muscular ballet dancer (the artist sucks at drawing guys with muscles) who fancies himself as a good, wise person who wants what's best for people when he's really just petty, manipulative and vindictive. For fun I did a <a href=\"http://yaoihuntresse.livejournal.com/11544.html\" target=\"_blank\">write-up of it</a> over 2 years ago. <br /> <br /> I'm sure some of you who go to the Comics Curmudgeon or are familiar with Comic Aligance's <a href=\"http://comicsalliance.com/tags/funky-winkerbean/\" target=\"_blank\">FunkyWatch</a> knows that Tom Batiuk's work (Funky Winkerbean and Crankshaft) is some of the most depressing stuff in the comic strip world. (At times it could compete with WoD.) When someone joked about the idea of Lisa (FW) being poisoned by her husband to cash off on her struggles, this idea wouldn't shut-up until I made a <a href=\"http://yaoihuntresse.livejournal.com/17499.html\" target=\"_blank\">Wraith write-up</a> for her. When I get an idea, it goes crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T23:07:28-08:00","id":45406,"title":"","content":"Jojo's Bizarre Adv.<br /> <br /> <b>Phantom Blood </b><br /> Dio Bando: Mortal to Lasombra<br /> Johnathan JoeStar: Mortal to Mage: Akashic Brotherhood (Using Life&amp; Prime Arcana) or Shih <br /> Will. Zeppeli: Akashic Brotherhood/ (Using Life&amp; Prime Arcana) or Shih<br /> Robert Speedwagon: Mortal to Hunter Bystander<br /> <br /> <b>Battle Tendancy</b><br /> Joseph JoeStar:&quot;NWOD&quot;Mage: Acanthus/Adamantine Arrow- Dorain (Using Prime &amp; Fate Arcana)<br /> Cesar Zeppelin:&quot;NWOD&quot; Mage: Obrimos/Adamantine Arrow -Perfected Adept (Using Force&amp; Prime Arcana)<br /> Lisa-Lisa:&quot;NWOD&quot; Mage: Obrimos/Adamantine Arrow -Perfected Adept (Using Matter&amp; Prime Arcana)<br /> Rudol von Stroheim: NWOD Hunter: Task Force Valkyrie<br /> Robert Speedwagon: NWOD Hunter:Cheiron Group<br /> Smokey Brown: Mortal: Innocent<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T13:18:53-08:00","id":45807,"title":"","content":"Full Metal Panic!<br /> <br /> Conversion Assumption: Mithril is like the Dies Ultimae, but run by Silver Fangs, mostly by their Kinfolk. Whispered operate as technomages, with a paradigm hemmed in by the Machine Incarna. Use of fighting robots is more limited, due to various issues with Weaver-tech.<br /> <br /> Sousuke: The Son of Bdshank's Tiger is... a weretiger. Dropped a lot of points into Willpower to make sure that he wouldn't go off the handle so easily. Replace scenes of people thinking that his weapons aren't real with incidents of relatively subdued Chatro mayhem covered up by the Delirium.<br /> Kaname: Orphan, has no desire to join mystical societies that would make her life change too much. Uses a paper fan as a focus for Mind magic without even really realizing it.<br /> Tessa: Orphan and Silver Fang Kinfolk. Has a Hakken-style arrangement* with her werewolf family in House Wyrmfoe.<br /> Melissa: Boli Zousizhe Kinfolk,<br /> Kurz: Glass Walker Kinfolk, had a mentor among the Dies Ultimae.<br /> Kalinin: Silver Fang Kinfolk<br /> Mardukas: Fianna Kinfolk<br /> Ben: Glass Walker Philodox<br /> Wraith: Gukutsuhi Kitsune<br /> <br /> Gauron: Former NWO combat agent, gone over to the SoE<br /> Xia twins: Consors to Gauron<br /> Gates: Marauder<br /> Leonard: Silver Fang Kinfolk who joined the Sons of Ether, thus falling out of favor with family.<br /> <br /> *The Hakken offer Mages who are Kin to them a choice - stay with their family, or join an organization of other mages and be practically dead to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:03:22-08:00","id":45955,"title":"","content":"Hellsing either OVA or the original <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/10r2rtu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1779-spider_one","name":"spider_one","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T09:01:24-08:00","id":46926,"title":"","content":"I remember years ago that someone made the start of a World of Darkness: Springfield (The Simpsons). Some friends (at the time) and I were building on the idea and here's some of the things that we came up with...<br /> <br /> -Springfield is pretty much where the Technocracy dumps all of it's losers. When you got a Progenitor like Dr. Nick Rivera and the NWO group, The Stone Cutters, (who are more interested in &quot;drinking beer and playing ping-pong&quot;) you can see why.<br /> -Mr. Burns is the Ventrue prince of Springfield who can only drink from people who are loyal to him. The ritual he uses &quot;to cheat death for another week&quot; (the episode where Homer thought he saw an alien) allows him resistance to the sun for a while. Of course, Smithers is a ghoul.<br /> -Professor Frink? Son of Ether all the way. Herb Powell (Homer's half-brother) may also be one.<br /> -Lisa could possibly be a hedge mage.<br /> -The Insanity Peppers are a magical creation of the Nuwisa (sp) that allow eater (even Mortals) to mentally enter an Umbral realm. The werecyotes will play around with the eater for a bit before giving them a quest that will grant them wisdom.<br /> -A Treehouse of Terror where Homer becomes a Mage and ends up pissing-off every Tradition he tries to join.<br /> <br /> Mage: Welcome to the Euthanos, Mr. Simpson.<br /> <br /> Homer: Can I kill Flanders?<br /> <br /> Mage: No, it is not his time on the Wheel of Life.<br /> <br /> Homer: Fine. I'm not joining some creepy death cult that won't let me kill Flanders.<br /> <br /> When the Technocracy won't take him in, Homer starts his own group. He gets a big head from his prestige and accidentally causes a major paradox backlash that forces the Traditions and Technocarcy to form an allegiance and in the end brings them closer together. So they both permanently lock Homer's powers and his and the town's memories away of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 01-11-2014, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T09:33:31-08:00","id":46941,"title":"","content":"Mr. Burns is a Methuselah,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T14:54:34-08:00","id":47082,"title":"","content":"Dexter Morgan is so a Euthie. Albeit a wayward one pretty close to a Quiet sometimes. (He talks to the Dead, although it could also be Manifest Avatar taking different forms to try and guide him) The whole show is revolving around his self discovery and retaining (regaining?) what little humanity he has to keep a normal cover. The Code he lives by is not far off from the Euthanatos Chadona, though it lacks the Chadona's complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar