ec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:30:11-08:00","id":47739,"title":"","content":"Going by supernatural-esqe urban fantasy animation shows, I've forgotten about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Dragon:_Jake_Long\" target=\"_blank\">American Dragon Jake Long</a>. While Jake Long and his family might be Zhong Lung (Mokole, while Jonathan Long is either kinfolk/human), I'm leaning more towards Changeling: the Dreaming with that show with all the other critters. That or the &quot;Dragon Council&quot; are under Changeling oath to protect and aid Changelings.<br /> Professor Hans Rotwood is an Arcanum member that is ignoring the whole &quot;Don't get too involved and close&quot; rule in trying to expose that supernatural creatures are real to the world.<br /> <br /> And man, would <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyles_%28TV_series%29\" target=\"_blank\">Gargoyles</a> be a massive CWOD crossover waiting to happen.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detentionaire\" target=\"_blank\">Detentionaire</a> (if you know a bit of it and the conspiracies) would be perfect for the Technocracy.<br /> Who wants to bet that the Red Tazelwurm is Lee Ping's Avatar and that he is a newly awakened mage in a Technocratic controlled school?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 01-12-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:11:50-08:00","id":47830,"title":"","content":"i will ask realdeadguy but...Would life on mars (SPOILERS)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> would be about a wraith being harrowed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T23:47:29-08:00","id":47977,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sleepy Hollow (Burton, 1999)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Lady Van Tassel</b><br /> A vindictive Verbena (why not) who uses the Spirit Sphere to compel the Wraith of the Hessian mercenary whose death she witnessed (and caused).<br /> <br /> <b>The Hessian</b><br /> A notorious mercenary in life, in death he has been enslaved by a vengeance seeking witch, acting as her otherworldly executioner. <br /> <br /> <u>Relics</u><br /> After his death, his favorite axe was briefly taken as a trophy. Shortly after, its carrier was slain and the axe destroyed, crossing the Shroud into the waiting hands of the Hessian.<br /> <br /> Although animals in the Shadowlands are rare, the Hessian\u2019s destrier was more than a possession; it was his only steady companion for the many campaigns he was contracted to fight in. As their lives and deaths were so closely linked, the Hessian\u2019s steed was waiting for him when Colonial forces finally laid him low.<br /> <br /> <u>Grave Goods</u><br /> After the Colonial minutemen killed and buried their unholy opponent, they marked the site of his grave with his own sword. In life, the sword was the source of his livelihood so it is fitting that the same weapon is also the marker for his death. This crossed the Shroud along with his beloved horse and trusty axe.<br /> <br /> <u>The Tree of the Dead</u><br /> At the site of his grave grew a twisted and gnarled skeleton of a tree. Whether from the festering anger of a seasoned warrior being unceremoniously slain or from a seed of evil planted by a young witch, none dare say. What is known is this site has become a Shallowing - a gateway between two worlds. The Shroud is significantly lower here than anywhere else in Sleepy Hollow. He uses this (at the witch\u2019s behest) to use Embody more effectively than would otherwise be possible.<br /> <br /> <u>His Skull</u><br /> In life, the Hessian knew he would be defeated one day. By an enemy musket, an opponent\u2019s blade, or perhaps time itself. He never imagined that we would suffer the indignity of being decapitated by his own sword. The Hessian\u2019s skull is his strongest Fetter to the Shadowlands and the Skinlands. The witch who controls him uses it now to compel his service. If he ever regains it, he will take her screaming into the Underworld.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","e