n-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=44373#post44373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Nicolas Cage in The Kiss of The Vampire, be a malkavian?</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't develop real fangs and seems less bothered by sunlight. I'd say he's a Malkavian ghoul. The Curse in his master's vitae has pushed him over the edge. The all of the urges that the &quot;lesser&quot; Beast of ghoul feels got directed to that one poor woman working for him. <br /> <br /> And, I love that movie. Nick Cage seemed to be the only person in the movie who understood how silly and terrible it was. He did a great job mocking it from the inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T12:18:02-08:00","id":60028,"title":"","content":"I figured Early Hickey (My Name is Earl) would be a Bone Gnawer Philodox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:56:28-08:00","id":62407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spider_one</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=45955#post45955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellsing either OVA or the original <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Alucard - 4th Generation Lasombra</i><br /> <br /> <i>Vlad Dracula, born 2<sup>nd</sup> in line to the throne of Walachia, was sent as a child to the Ottomans</i><i> as a hostage where he was physically and sexually abused. He would go on to defeat a Hungarian usurper to the throne in hand to hand combat and then waged war against the Turks. He became known as the Vlad the Impaler for his execution of traitorous nobles. \u201cDied\u201d in battle against the Turks outside of Bucharest. Claims that as he lay dying he lapped up the blood of the fallen and through sheer willpower and hatred transformed himself into a vampire.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla believe his existence proves that Lasombra survived his assassination attempt as claimed by Montano. After brainwashing Gratiano, it is likely he wandered eastern Europe for a time, coming across Dracula as he lay hallucinating and dying. Impressed with his sheer will to survive, he was embraced. For the next four centuries he ran wild in the Balkans, supporting rebellions against the Ottomans, terrorizing the Turks and battling any kindred who got in his way. It was during this period that Dracula became known as the Scourge of the Assamites, as he identified them with the Ottoman conquerors. </i><br /> <br /> <i>The Lasombra have repeatedly tried to assassinate him, his very existence lends credence to Montano\u2019s claim that Lasombra lives and the Sabbat \u2018publicly\u2019 insists that when he was embraced he was only of the 5<sup>th</sup> generation, perhaps a childer of Montano himself. If he\u2019s now of the 4<sup>th</sup>, they argue he must have gained such power through diablerie. The Tzimisce who regarded Eastern Europe as their personal territory constantly tried to eliminate him, and their failure gnaws at them to this day. While not particularly attracted to the institutions of the Camarilla, the enmity of the two main pillars of the Sabbat drove Dracula to be loosely affiliated with it, where he was viewed as a significant asset in the war against the Sabbat, despite being an unpredictable loose cannon. </i><br /> <br /> <i>After the Russo-Turkish War of 1877-78 led to the independence of Walachia and Moldavia, Dracula went on a \u2018victory\u2019 tour of Europe. Defeated and captured by the Demon Hunter Abraham Van Hellsing, he was bound by sorcery to obey the Hellsing line in perpetuity and renamed Alucard. The Camarilla suspects he could break such an enchantment if he wished, and will refrain from doing so only as long as he respects his \u201cmaster\u201d. It is well known that he finds being the attack dog of the British crown immensely entertaining. </i><br /> <br /> <i>The Camarilla tolerates this situation because Hellsing keeps the Masquerade. Alucard is the unofficial Scourge of the British Isles, cleansing them of the Sabbat, Anarchs, Lupines, Infernalists and anyone who threatens the Masquerade. Of course, in truth the reality of the matter was that they couldn't hope to stop him, for his power had grown like nothing seen since the days of old when the antideluvians reigned over their progeny in the second city. Just over five hundred years old, he is already more than a match for Methuselah ten times his age.<br /> <br /> In torpor from 1969-89, he was woken by his current master Integra Hellsing. Was pivotal in defeating the Nazi Vampire invasion of 1998 that blew the masquerade wide open, climaxing in a duel with the mad Gangrel Methuselah called Schr\u00f6dinger. A few months prior he sired a fledgling, a young policewoman named Seras Victoria. This is a development that is at odds with his growing disillusionment with immortality. He privately wishes to be slain by a mortal man, believing that is how all great monsters come to an end. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-01-2014, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:53:11-08:00","id":62611,"title":"","content":"So would that make Anderson an Inquistor, a Celestial Chorus Mage or a Hunter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.th