gh Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T23:59:22-07:00","id":210920,"title":"","content":"THE POWER OF GAIA COMPELLS YOU!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T06:00:42-07:00","id":211130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Iron Man - Technocracy. Just not sure which group. </div> </div> </div>Void Engineers. He is not not stuck up enough for Iteration X.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:24:37-07:00","id":211713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=210733#post210733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...lets go into something much...Evil...<br /> Bella Swan, Jacob Black, Edward Cullen and Shotgun Dad (bella swan dad).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except for Bella and the elder Swan, Hobgoblins. Bella herself is the Marauder generating the &quot;supernatural creatures&quot; as a way to escape from her life before she moved to Queens (I think that's the town..), due to psychotic bullying that rendered her more or less persona-less except for basic human urges. Charlie (Shotgun Dad) is an Imbued who doesn't know that insane Mages can generate supernatural creatures out of sheer crazy, and upon learning of the vampires is too busy going WTF and doing research on Kindred that sparkle instead of burn in the sun to really involve himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T10:34:05-07:00","id":214800,"title":"","content":"Rosangela Blackwell from the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackwell_%28series%29\" target=\"_blank\">Blackwell series</a> by <a href=\"http://www.wadjeteyegames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Wadjet Eye Games</a>.<br /> <br /> 1) On the first glance - a Sin-Eater, just doing her job of helping confused Ghosts/Wraiths to come up with their new &quot;state&quot; and move on to Eternity.<br /> <br /> 2) As the series progress, she becomes more like Awakened Mage (Euthanatoi, probably), strengthening her connection with the Universe and becoming aware of some global plots (Joe Gould's theory of interconnection) as part of her Seekings and doing some epic-level stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 10-02-2014, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T12:23:03-07:00","id":214970,"title":"","content":"ok, characters from Lord of the Rings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T18:18:27-07:00","id":217712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=214970#post214970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, characters from Lord of the Rings</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imbued, mostly.<br /> <br /> Gandalf would be an Elohim that hasn't Fallen but accepts strictures on his power to directly interact with the world, Saruman one in the process of Falling, and Sauron after rematerializing himself an Earthbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T01:53:14-07:00","id":217978,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lord of the Rings, Black Dog Style!</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&quot;It began with the forging of the Great Rings. Three were given to the Balorians, immortal, demented and most perverted of all beings. Seven to the Spiral-Lords, great warlords and witches of the Hives. And nine, nine rings were gifted to the race of Caine, who above all else desire power. For within these rings was the bound the strength and the will to dominate each race. But they were all of them deceived, for another ring was made. Far in the land Mordor, in the Light of Mount Destiny, the Lightbringer Sauron forged a master ring in secret, and into this ring he poured his benevolence, his compassion and his will to let all life flourish. One ring to free them all.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Coalition of the Ring</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Frodo Brakkins:</b> <br /> A reclusive boggart who lives in the marshes of the Slum. When it\u2019s discovered that his belligerent drunk of an uncle has unwittingly uncovered the Lightbringer\u2019s ring, he undertakes a quest (for which he will be handsomely rewarded with hookers and blow) to destroy the Lightbringer\u2019s blessed ring and keep Sauron from freeing the subjugated peoples of Middle Earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Samwiz Gangrene</b>: <br /> Enslaved at a young age, Frodo\u2019s thrall is dragged through treacherous terrain and forced to do horrible things for unspeakable amounts of money on their way to Mount Destiny.<br /> <br /> <b>Aragorn, Childe of Arathorn:</b><br /> Heir to the Voivode\u2019s throne of the Black City of Gondor, the young Tzimisce journeys with Frodo to make sure the hapless Glamour-filled juice-sack does what he\u2019s supposed to do instead of selling out to the Lightbringer. Not that good guys have a lot of spare change, but it\u2019s better to be safe than sorry.<br /> <br /> <b>Boromir, Murder-General of the Black Tower: </b><br /> Childe to Denethor, the Regent of Gondor. Although an accomplished warrior in life, the honorable Keeper has not been able to let go of his vestigial warrior\u2019s code. He follows Aragorn with a weak veneer of loyalty, secretly hoping to obtain the ring for the Lightbringer and bring peace to Middle Earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Legolas Rotlead:</b><br /> Prince of House Balor. A master of the strange magic known as boomsticks, Legolas lends his pistols to the Coalition so that his people may continue their predations on the lands surrounding Mirkwood.<br /> <br /> <b>Gorehowl, Son of Gloin:</b><br /> The rapacious Black Spiral Dancer has left the confines of the mountain Hives and joined the Coalition of the Ring. Over the course the journey, he becomes close to his traveling companion of House Balor. Very close. &lt;wink wink nudge nudge&gt;<br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T18:59:55-07:00","id":219731,"title":"","content":"*snerk*<br /> <br /> Okay, how about introducing a lot of you to something new? What would the Undersiders, the main teenage supervillain(?) team of <u><a href=\"http://parahumans.wordpress.com/table-of-contents/\" target=\"_blank\">Worm</a></u> be?<br /> <br /> For those of you intimidated by THREE NOVELS' WORTH OF CHAPTERS, here's the basic rundown:<br /> <br /> <b>Skitter, aka Taylor Hebert: </b>Lonely, slightly paranoid and depressed nerd empress of insects. Capable of controlling and hijacking the perceptions of every arthropod in a set area by thinking about it, has the multitasking abilities this requires, and is later revealed as a genius strategist.<br /> <br /> <b>Grue, aka Brain Laiborn: </b>Honorable and friendly teenage mercenary. Darkness generator, can see just fine in his own cloud and debuffs any powers that enter it, along with feelings of touch. Later gains the ability to actually steal the powers of capes who enter the darkzone, while they're in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tattletale, aka Lisa Wilbourn: </b>Snarky, manipulative and actually rather kindhearted (to people she actually knows) tactician and planner. Her power turns her into Blonde Sherlock Holmes, to the point of being able to pretend she's a telepath because she's that good at reading people.<br /> <br /> <b>Bitch, aka Rachel Lindt: </b>Before you ask; <i>she </i>calls herself that, which should give you an idea of how misanthropic she tends to be. Has the ability to summon organic power armor for her dogs, turning them into enormous, resilient kaiju. She can't directly control them though, she's just really good at training them.<br /> <br /> <b>Regent, aka Alec: </b>Mildly sociopathic and even more snarky body puppeteer. Given time, he can turn an opponent's nervous system into what might as well be a second body for him over the range of several miles, in a pinch he can make someone punch themselves out.<br /> <br /> <b>Imp, aka Aisha Laiborn: </b>The above Laiborn's little sister, and the epitome of snark, and mischief. Living perception filter, if she wants to she can make you forget she exists even as she's kicking you in the nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18