25,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=331592#post331592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok....Dipper, Mabel, Stan, Soos, Wendy, Lil Gideon, Bill Cypher, Giffany and Gravity Falls as a location.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, it's funny; I'm actually planning on doing a Gravity Falls crossover fic with the nWoD, after my winter exams are done. Featuring a canon tween werewolf (Mark &quot;Little Shadow&quot; Lee, from Wolfsbane). So this is within my interests.<br /> <br /> As for the characters;<br /> <br /> Pines Family and Employees of the Shack: Tier 1 Vigil Hunters, one and all. The one time Dipper tried to use supernatural power, it was powered by a Journal, and it backfired horribly. I'm not discounting Stan from being a Son of Ether, though.<br /> <br /> Lil' Gideon: Sorcerer who's adept at pretending to be a Mage. He's also terrible at Mind and anything related.<br /> <br /> Bill Cipher: Incarna of some sort, though it's honestly up for grabs whether he's aligned with the Wyld or the Wyrm. Could be a Dreaming Fae who has never, and will never, become a changeling, too.<br /> <br /> Giffany: Also a spirit, though a much less powerful one. She's not aligned to the Weaver despite her technological origin, though, she's too emotional (way too emotional) for that.<br /> <br /> Gravity Falls: World's Largest Overlap With The Umbra, Whatever Those Are Called. Not aligned to any of the Triat in particular, or maybe it's a huge Locus aligned to the concept and emotion of Wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 12-07-2014, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T19:29:42-08:00","id":340363,"title":"","content":"would Five Nights at Freddies be the story of five childrens which animatronic bodies became their Fetters, what kind of wraith would they be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:21:02-08:00","id":342924,"title":"","content":"I've been jonesing to run a Mage/Werewolf Deep Umbra game based on...<br /> <br /> Superjail!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.