Stripling (same with the three child spirits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T09:14:09-08:00","id":365468,"title":"","content":"Not fictional, but I think Adam Sandler would be a Faustian Devil and the actors in his Happy Madison productions made pacts with him. They still have careers, but they have to be in bad movies for the rest of their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T11:45:40-08:00","id":365564,"title":"","content":"ok..what about dilbert? does he works for Pentex, or for some incompetent technocratic agency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T03:57:09-08:00","id":366191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=362492#post362492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the Tall Man from Phantasm?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we learn of his past in <b>Phantasm III: Lord of the Dead</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wu0a_XOxRlM\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>), I'd say he's a Difference Engineer <i>barrabi </i>(i.e. an early Virtual Adept who's joined the Nephandi), probably from the late Nineteenth Century (based on his tech). Judging from the 2 brothers flashback, we're talking about a character who was fascinated by the idea that humans might be able to exist purely as brains (with the right support equipment), and communicate directly mind-to-mind. And as he grew older, he became convinced that he could &quot;hack&quot; death, and built an experimental portal to &quot;the afterlife&quot;. He entered the prototype (apparently) as a kindly old man . . . and came back as the Tall Man.<br /> <br /> That just sounds like a mage obsessed with the Ahl-i-Batin's &quot;Web of Faith&quot; (telepathic network) . . . like the early Difference Engineers. And if his experiments with the portal were unauthorized . . . well, the Technocracy doesn't teach the rank-and-file about &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; (i.e. the Spirit sphere), so he'd have had no idea about the dangers of the &quot;Other Side&quot;. . . And the Nephandi Cauls would certainly explain the changes in his personality and appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-11-2015, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T04:35:41-08:00","id":366196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=57906#post57906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would robocop be a risen with some help of the pentex or the technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't seen the new version, but classic Robocop would (probably) be an Iteration X cyborg . . .but a prototype version commissioned by the Syndicate as a &quot;cost-effective&quot; way to &quot;upgrade and recycle damaged knowledge assets&quot; (I.e. cops crippled in the line of duty). Hence the reason his bionics seem so clunky (compared to standard Iteration cyborgs) - the Syndicate is going for cheap, and (hopefully) plausible* under consensual reality<br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">after all, everyone &quot;<i>knows&quot;</i> that new technological devices tend to be bulky, awkward, and with a lot of room for improvement. Why should the &quot;first&quot; cyborg be any different?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-11-2015, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T20:55:49-08:00","id":366930,"title":"","content":"So, tell me, what of Myotismon from Digimon? He's obviously a vampire, but which clan would be belong to?<br /> <br /> The most obvious answers to me are one of three clans: Tzimisce, Gangrel, or Tremere. Not sure which one of those three though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T21:56:02-08:00","id":366972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=366930#post366930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, tell me, what of Myotismon from Digimon? He's obviously a vampire, but which clan would be belong to?<br /> <br /> The most obvious answers to me are one of three clans: Tzimisce, Gangrel, or Tremere. Not sure which one of those three though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce Koldun i belive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T03:17:14-08:00","id":367183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=347974#post347974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one explain Marceline the Vampire Queen? Obviously she's one of the few kindred survivors of some kind of mage war, fae invasion gehenna apocalypse scenario, but what exactly is she?<br /> <br /> That giant tentacle monster form would seem to indicate Vicissitude 9, but she has the Lasombra flaw. She also has very high levels of fortitude, protean, necromancy and thaumaturgy. And then there's the fact that she was &amp;quot;half-demon&amp;quot; before she was embraced. How would that even work??</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's a fan of Adventure Time here? Or is the half demon part just inexplicable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T07:49:55-08:00","id":367357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=367183#post367183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one's a fan of Adventure Time here? Or is the half demon part just inexplicable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons, as in D:TF demons, cannot reproduce, so you'd have to go with half-spirit of some other kind. Which, naturally, would produce issues with the Embrace. The classic WoD games, they're just not as permissive as AT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:35:54-08:00","id":369201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=365564#post365564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok..what about dilbert? does he works for Pentex, or for some incompetent technocratic agency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . Dilbert? I'd go one of two ways. Either he's an Orphan technomancer (that is, a science-paradigm mage who doesn't belong to a faction), possibly newly Awakened, who doesn't understand why his fellow engineers (and humans) suddenly seem so slow, untalented, and generally incompetent. After all, if he can build such amazing machines, shouldn't everyone?<br /> <br /> Or he's a knocker (changeling kith with a knack for machinery) trying to hold down a job in a mundane/human corporation. Under normal circumstances, knockers generally don't play well with others, and trying to maintain a job in such a banality rich environment . .. well, it would explain a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T09:00:56-08:00","id":369785,"title":"","content":"Hm, time to offer my own-<br /> <br /> Dangan Ronpa, either 1 or 2. Monokuma must be included,<br /> <br /> (the Mastermind doesn't need to be, I can't see how you would be able to interpret them as anything but a Nephandus of some stripe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T10:36:24-08:00","id":369850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=365468#post365468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not fictional, but I think Adam Sandler would be a Faustian Devil and the actors in his Happy Madison productions made pacts with him. They still have careers, but they have to be in bad movies for the rest of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would explain <i><b>SO MUCH</b></i>, even Grown Ups 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:53:37-08:00","id":371150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=369850#post369850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would explain <i><b>SO MUCH</b></i>, even Grown Ups 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Next time I'm running a WoD game I'm going to have <i>every</i> splat working together to destroy that wretched, utterly irredeemably corrupt abomination spawned from the deepest, blackest pit of the most nightmarish of hells.<br /> <br /> And we'll get that demon too.<br /> <br /> If there's time. After all priorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T19:23:17-08:00","id":373968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=347974#post347974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one explain Marceline the Vampire Queen? Obviously she's one of the few kindred survivors of some kind of mage war, fae invasion gehenna apocalypse scenario, but what exactly is she?<br /> <br /> That giant tentacle monster form would seem to indicate Vicissitude 9, but she has the Lasombra flaw. She also has very high levels of fortitude, protean, necromancy and thaumaturgy. And then there's the fact that she was &quot;half-demon&quot; before she was embraced. How would that even work??</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take a shot at it, but with the following caveat - we're missing key biographical information about Marceline. So later seasons may invalidate this analysis.<br /> <br /> <i>Adventure Time</i> introduces Marceline as an incredibly territorial vampire with the ability to turn into a giant bat monster . . . which is pretty much a textbook Tzimisce. The whole bat-monster form is the level 6 power of Vicissitude. And she was a child during the Great Mushroom War (which occurred roughly a thousand years ago). So she's a Tzimisce methusaleh of at least 7th generation (or else she wouldn't be able to learn level 6 powers).<br /> <br /> Given the way the series portrays her: one serious boyfriend, playing in a garage band, shave your head just &quot;because&quot; . . . I'm going to guess she was embraced between the ages of 17 and 20. Old enough to be cool in the eyes of Finn (who's ca. 14), and old enough to be comfortable in her skin, but not old enough to have a truly adult vibe. Of course, the whole post-apocalypse, living for a thousand years thing is going to skew things . . .but that's still roughly where I'd place her.<br /> <br /> And speaking of that boyfriend - Ash appears to be a Tremere (or maybe a wannabe). We see him use blood magic several times in the show, and in a post-apocalyptic world, who's going to complain about a Tzimisce shacking up with a Tremere. So Marceline could easily have learned some magic off him.<br /> <br /> As for the whole &quot;tentacle monster&quot; thing, I don't think that was her at all, but instead her father's amulet. Finn turns into almost the exact same creature, too, when he puts it on.<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> Now for the hard part - the whole &quot;half-demon&quot; thing. Marceline is the daughter of Hunsen Aberdeer, demonic ruler of the Nightosphere (an Umbral realm of chaos and suffering). And, in the World of Darkness, true demons can't have kids (although some banes can). Yet, as we see in the Simon &amp; Marcie flashbacks, Marcelline never looks like a normal human child. Her skin's blue-grey, and she has pointed ears, for example.<br /> <br /> However, if you look at Hunsen Aberdeer and how he lives . . . I don't think he's a demon (or a bane) at all. With his yellow-red eyes and blue-gray skin, he looks nothing like his subjects. Plus, his home looks like it came right out of an early '80s sitcom: refrigerator, comfy recliner, tv . . . None of which matches anything in the Nightosphere, but which does scream &quot;former human&quot;. And given that he has powerful magical artifacts lying around . . . .<br /> <br /> My guess is that Hunsen Aberdeer is actually a former mage who turned himself into his current form in the search for immortality (god only knows he wouldn't be the first WoD mage to do so). And he just decided to call himself a demon afterwards. That would explain the artifacts (and the lack of personal magic), the very human lifestyle, and (probably) the fact that he can father children who are close enough to stock humanity to be embraced.<br /> <br /> Again, though, we're still missing key details about Marcelline's mother, and her sire (assuming they aren't the same person). And its still possible that <i>Adventure Time </i>will throw us another curveball or two about her past. But this analysis works with what we know (at least right now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T19:42:01-08:00","id":373975,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's only the amulet, but I'd have rewatch the episodes she's in.<br /> <br /> She's definitely at least sixth generation since she can phase through walls and that's a Protean 7 power.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just watching the first two episodes she appears in, and aside from her giant bat form she also turns into a werewolf like monster and a reptilian/snake monster so she either knows doppelganger (Vicissitude 9) or she'd also need to know Shape of the Beast's Wrath (Protean 7) and a high level Serpentis ability (Apep's Semblance maybe? That's an 8th level ability). Best to keep it simple and say she's simply mastered Vicissitude. Especially since she uses Vicissitude on Finn's arms without touching him in the Henchman episode, which is an 8th level ability (will over form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-18-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:53:04-08:00","id":374031,"title":"","content":"How about one from the Cthulhu mythos? Anyone want to take a stab at Randolph Carter? Is he a mage, a changeling, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T07:27:33-08:00","id":374271,"title":"","content":"<