theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T13:36:35-07:00","id":483825,"title":"","content":"&quot;<b>The 13th Warrior</b> &quot;<br /> <br /> Ahmed Ibn Fahdlan: Silent Strider<br /> Buliwyf: Get of Fenris (All of Buliwyf's crew are Get)<br /> Herger the Joyous: Get of Fenris &quot; Ragabash&quot;<br /> Wigliff: Shadowlord<br /> King Hrothgar: Silver Fang<br /> <br /> The Wendo: Black Spiral Dancers<br /> <br /> This whole movie screams WTA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T10:29:35-07:00","id":484727,"title":"","content":"what exactly would be The Queen of The Damned, an antediluvian or a matussaleh?, and what clan?<br /> the headless horseman from sleepy hollow (the tv show)<br /> Santiago, the vampires from the theatre and louis from Interview with a vampire<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T21:59:35-07:00","id":485079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Queen of The Damned, an antediluvian or a matussaleh? </div> </div> </div>She is her own settings Caine basically, being the first Vampire whose fate is tied to the whole race. Clan? It's been a while since I read the novels but based on her personality perhaps Toreador would be the best fit, just like with Lestat though Lestats mother whom he embraced would be Gangrel as that setting has no Clans and an individuals personality determines more about one's Clan equivalent in VtM terms.<br /> <br /> Santiago and the rest are of the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vampires crew if going with the movie Santiago he could be Malkavian but I'd still err on the side of Toreadors for the most part. But like said it has been quite a while since I read the books so I do not have a clear handle on such side characters at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> headless horseman from sleepy hollow (the tv show) </div> </div> </div>In it's own setting it is a forerunner of the apocalypse being one of the Four Horsemen so it's a bit hard to pin down in WoD terms, a Talon of the Wyrm perhaps? But if going by the character itself instead of it's role in the series it would fit as a Risen most clearly as they can easily pull of the headless part along with the stamina to handle quite a bit of heavy fire etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:32:48-07:00","id":486497,"title":"","content":"Weren't the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vampires pretty much the basis for the Sabbat when White Wolf was getting started?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=476523#post476523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would BOB and The Giant from Twin Peaks be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think BOB was clearly a demon of one variety or another - I don't remember anything implying that he had ever been human. I guess the giant and the Man from Another Place would both be spirits in some umbral court.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:35:03-07:00","id":495723,"title":"","content":"Pennywise aka IT is a trapped bane bound by the 3 brothers or an Earthbound Demon.<br /> Haven't seen or read Under the Dome I'm behind on my King readings.<br /> Carrie White- I would go with Aberrant. Or possibly an Orphan Mage.<br /> Roland a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T21:43:10-07:00","id":497085,"title":"","content":"Alice and the rest of the characters from Alice in Wonderland.<br /> <br /> Hellboy and the BPRD (hopefully the comic)<br /> <br /> Pinhead and the Cenobites, as well the Lament Configuration<br /> <br /> Dorothy, The Scarecrow, The Cowardly Lion, The Thinman, the Wicked Witch of the West and the Wizard of Oz<br /> <br /> Peter Pan and Captain Hook<br /> <br /> Dc's Tim Hunter<br /> <br /> Ash Williams (Evil Dead, Evil Dead II , Army of Darkness)<br /> <br /> and what Generation and disciplines would the Count Orlok have (In both Nosferatu and In The Shadow of the Vampire)<br /> <br /> Ok, Here comes the curb ball. Doctor Frank N' Further and The Rocky Horror<br /> <br /> And the Cast of Mystery Science Theatre 3000 (Mike, Joe, Crow , Tom , The Satellite of Love, Dr Forrester , Dr Erhard , TV's Frank , Pearl Forrester, Bobo and Brain guy )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 04-30-2015, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T22:17:51-07:00","id":540589,"title":"","content":"ok this one is easy<br /> <br /> Explain the Five nights at freddys mythos in WoD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:13:22-07:00","id":541396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=540589#post540589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok this one is easy<br /> <br /> Explain the Five nights at freddys mythos in WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone claimed that M20 had Pentex buying some HIT Mark Vs. That'd be a fairly robust start; the remainder is taken up by a fairly straightforward story of revenge and the waiting game from Wraith, as child ghosts try desperately to keep their Shadows under check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T03:49:06-07:00","id":559210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=497085#post497085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alice and the rest of the characters from Alice in Wonderland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alice is a newly awake changeling, probably on the border between childling (kid) and wilder (teenager). &quot;Wonderland&quot; is the fief of the Queen of Hearts, a sidhe monarch deep in Bedlam . . . and one whom no one has tried to depose yet. Her madness is ripping the fiefdom apart, to the point that no one realizes that Alice is new, untrained and without her Saining. So Alice just wanders through the local Dreaming, stopping at various freeholds, in search of a talking chimera in the shape of a white rabbit. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pinhead and the Cenobites, as well the Lament Configuration </div> </div> </div>Pinhead and the Cenobites are kuei-jin <i>akuma</i>, in service to the Yama King known as Leviathan. <b>Hellraiser III</b> recounts how the man who became Pinhead sought damnation after World War I, and found it in east Asia. Tortured by Leviathan (and its minions), the now undead Pinhead buys moments of solace by helping damn others . . . although on some level, he still craves the pain himself. Oh, and the monstrous appearance that he (and the other cenobites) have is just a form of demon shintai<br /> <br /> As for the magic puzzle box known as the Lamentation Configuration, its a mystic artifact, the result of an accidental collaboration between a technomage and a Nephandus (see <b>Bloodlines</b>), which permits direct access to Leviathan's Yomi (hell) realm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Peter Pan and Captain Hook </div> </div> </div>Neverland is a realm in the Dreaming, reached by taking the trod found by following the second star to the right, and going straight on till morning. Two changelings contest control of the realm - a wilder sidhe from House Fiona known as Peter Pan, and an Unseelie sidhe grump (house unknown) known as Captain Hook. Both sidhe have enchanted mortal followers, while Peter Pan also has the support of a Never (chimerical pixie) known as Tinkerbelle. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, Here comes the curb ball. Doctor Frank N' Further and The Rocky Horror </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . If I had to guess, Doctor Frank'n'Furter is a Son of Ether on the brink of going Marauder<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:22:51-07:00","id":560724,"title":"","content":"I could see Daria Morgandorfer (sp) being a hedge mage (both pre and post spin-off series). Post-Beavis and Butt-head Daria could also end up like that one Nosferatu template (Morbid Artist Vindictively Embraced) where her sire is annoyed with her elitist, against everything moppiness and gives her something to really angst over. Quinn and/or Britney would either be some Anarch Catorie's Mortal pawn or blood doll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T00:51:28-07:00","id":565077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=540589#post540589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok this one is easy<br /> <br /> Explain the Five nights at freddys mythos in WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been toying with this one for a while, and even have a potential scenario for it.<br /> <br /> The animatronics are just that - animatronics, albeit perhaps advanced ones. They may, in fact, have been designed by some technosorcerer with the Path of Enchantment.<br /> <br /> Fazbear Entertainment is of course a subsidiary of Pentex, but it's not a major branch by any means. In fact, its only &quot;in the know&quot; employee is a young exec who is just high enough in the Pentex hierarchy to know they serve the Wyrm, and some little bits about the supernatural. He noticed that, after those kids went missing, the animatronics have been acting up. You know, wandering where they aren't supposed to, staring at people, committing homicide on the night guards (and at least once taking a bite out of someone, leading to brain damage). Of course the suits are possessed by Wraiths of the children who hold a grudge against the Purple Man, but our Pentex minor exec doesn't know what a Wraith is. He just assumes the suits are possessed by some of those &quot;Bane&quot; things he sometimes hears about. And since the Wyrm apparently loves Banes and uses them to spread misery, he just goes along with the situation, quietly disposing of dead bodies, insisting the animatronics be allowed to roam the halls at night, and even actively making it harder for the guards to avoid getting killed. Sure, it means high turnover, but that's a given in the food service industry, and if it makes the Wyrm happy then it's all good.<br /> <br /> The game scenario, then, would be that the players investigating the rash of disappearances. Perhaps one of the party members' friends disappears, and that player character applies for the job to get to the bottom of it. A Mage game might make it too easy - if anyone has Spirit 2 it's almost insultingly so. But it might make for a good mystery, with the Child Wraiths asking the Mages to find who killed them and bring him to justice...preferably their justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T20:43:33-07:00","id":567290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=42665#post42665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highschool of the Dead. They're mostly hunters... mostly. For some reason, I want to say that Takashi is a wolf among the sheep, if you will. Or perhaps a tiger or crow. If not, a Judge that managed to get a few Wayward powers.<br /> <br /> Hisashi: Visionary. But not so gifted with foresight, more of the leader type you would expect. Fails to foresee that not carrying a weapon when you are amidst a bunch of zombies and relying on hand to hand combat expertise is a bad idea, but perhaps as one of the Balancers, he might develop Cleave to justify it and last longer?<br /> <br /> Saeko: Martyr. Feels that she is just as bad as the monsters she fights.<br /> <br /> Shizuka: Redeemer. She uses Bluster by screaming in a panic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm going for a redo on those two. Depending on how you want to take the scene at the shrine, either Takashi is a Visionary with the Conviction-bootstrapping Edge and Saeko is a Wayward who isn't quite so thrilled about being a Wayward, or Takashi is a Redeemer and Saeko is a weretiger with the Night Pryio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T01:45:29-07:00","id":567594,"title":"","content":"Highschool of the Dead is such a guilty pleasure...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T11:34:32-07:00","id":568203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=567594#post567594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highschool of the Dead is such a guilty pleasure...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like the Wayward creed book, if the Wayward creed book was packed to the brim with fan service and reveling in a Mad Max-type situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-25-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:36:08-07:00","id":572464,"title":"","content":"Did you see the lovely full color oversized hardcovers? I actually got both. The manga is quite a bit better then the anime, as that thing just devolved into fan service and improbable boob physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:50:11-07:00","id":578324,"title":"","content":"What about the shamans from Shaman King?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5176-curlyinsaneguy","name":"CurlyInsaneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T03:21:23-07:00","id":578488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CurlyInsaneGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=578324#post578324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the shamans from Shaman King?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . interesting question. Yoh and most of his friends partner with the spirits of the dead, and they fit fairly well into the wraith framework. They'd need Possession, of course . . . but otherwise, that works fairly well. Arguably, they even have fetters and Passions. <br /> <br /> As for the shamans themselves . . . I'm tempted to go &quot;mage&quot; - possibly a variant on Dreamspeakers. That would explain how they can manifest their spirits, and a fear of paradox would explain why so many of the fights take place away from prying eyes. Heck, they're vulgar enough to make certamen seem coincidental (by comparison, at least). Plus the Patch tribe's &quot;home&quot; (where they hold the later rounds of the tournament) appears to be in a pocket dimension.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:30:52-07:00","id":585764,"title":"","content":"How about some of the characters/creatures from Shadow heart 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T16:13:45-08:00","id":786321,"title":"","content":"ok....<br /> <br /> Star Wars Characters (Non expanded universe, all 6 movies)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:29:01-08:00","id":786404,"title":"","content":"Ok, not sure if this has been said yet but, the Winchester brothers are clearly Mummies. Some low key, nifty tricks for the most part, keep coming back from the dead, are frequently in contact with the divine, and they fight evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T21:19:11-08:00","id":786489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=786404#post786404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, not sure if this has been said yet but, the Winchester brothers are clearly Mummies. Some low key, nifty tricks for the most part, keep coming back from the dead, are frequently in contact with the divine, and they fight evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A good stab, but their whole bit is that they're human. Let's go for something a bit more on point. They're Hunters, obviously, originally with the Union. How do they not stay dead? A ten point Merit I like to call &quot;God is My Co-Author,&quot; that basically allows them to keep cheating death, but only so long as they take some truly nasty flaws and/or derangements that they have to work to resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:12:03-08:00","id":786703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=786489#post786489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A good stab, but their whole bit is that they're human. Let's go for something a bit more on point. They're Hunters, obviously, originally with the <b>Union</b>. How do they not stay dead? A ten point Merit I like to call &quot;God is My Co-Author,&quot; that basically allows them to keep cheating death, but only so long as they take some truly nasty flaws and/or derangements that they have to work to resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The aptly-named Splat Not Appearing In This Collection of Universes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:52:00-08:00","id":786723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=786703#post786703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The aptly-named Splat Not Appearing In This Collection of Universes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OH yes, that's CoD. Then drop the Union part, and replace with &quot;collection of working class joes who've networked together to share information and support.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:27:59-08:00","id":792132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=367357#post367357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons, as in D:TF demons, cannot reproduce, so you'd have to go with half-spirit of some other kind. Which, naturally, would produce issues with the Embrace. The classic WoD games, they're just not as permissive as AT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things in the mythic age were more flexible,but when magic and the fae faded from the world things solidified and the various supernaturals got a lot more stratified. However it seems that there was masquerade breaking magic being thrown around in the AT timeline even before the apocalypse, so things may have gone more flexible towards the &quot;end times&quot; again. At leadt that's how I'd hand wave things.<br /> <br /> Edit: was browsing this thread for the first time in ten months when I responded to this. Forgot this was more discussion of the topic on the next page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 12-24-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:45:12-08:00","id":795022,"title":"","content":"Ok...<br /> What would the characters of the Gran Morrison's comig &quot;The Invisibles&quot; be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T08:28:36-08:00","id":801408,"title":"","content":"Ok, i got an interesting one here..<br /> <br /> The Overlook Hotel. Both from the Novel and The Movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:50:19-08:00","id":806079,"title":"","content":"One time my friends and I did a Hunter: The Reckoning play-by-post game where we played as Naruto characters redone as Imbued. This is what all we came up with, though it may not be exactly faithful to canon on either end.<br /> <br /> <b>Naruto Uzumaki: </b>Defender<br /> <b>Hinata Hyuga: </b>Innocent<br /> <b>Kiba Inuzuka: </b>Avenger<br /> <b>Shikamaru Nara: </b>Visionary<br /> <b>Mikoto Uchiha: </b>Martyr<br /> <b>Sasuke Uchiha: </b>Wayward<br /> <b>Tsunade: </b>Judge<br /> <br /> <br /> Thought it might be worth mentioning in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:54:19-08:00","id":806235,"title":"","content":"The Hyuga bloodline power is really more on par with the Judgment Edge Discern, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:19:30-08:00","id":806635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=801408#post801408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i got an interesting one here..<br /> <br /> The Overlook Hotel. Both from the Novel and The Movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Stephen King's work translates well into <b>Changeling</b>. Now, you could argue that the Overlook Hotel (or the mansion Rose Red) are haunts full of particularly malign wraiths (or even Spectres) . . . but they work better as freeholds. Horrific nightmares are as much a part of the Dreaming as sweet dreams, and there are canon examples of some very messed-up freeholds (I'm looking at you, Graymere Glen). The prowling topiaries, the fact that (in the early days) Jack almost instantly forgets his encounters, even his wigging out and typing nothing but &quot;all work and no play makes Jack a dull boy&quot; for hundreds of pages . . . <i>Changeling</i> has rules to cover all of that. <br /> <br /> And it wouldn't be out of place to have wraiths haunting a freehold. Thanks to all the faerie-inspired &quot;fun and games&quot;, the Shroud between the Skin and Shadowlands can be <i>very</i> thin, even in the happier/ more pleasant ones. And the darker ones . . . It makes perfect sense for some of them to push a vulnerable human into murder (or worse). After all, to enter a freehold is to walk into a place where dreams are made real. And people have dreamt some very black dreams, down through the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:51:14-08:00","id":809052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=795022#post795022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...<br /> What would the characters of the Gran Morrison's comig &quot;The Invisibles&quot; be?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, Mages, honestly. Each of them does magic in their own way - King Mob uses a neo-Shamanic style combined with drug- and sex-magic (I'd probably make him a Dual Trad Dreamspeaker/Cult of Ecstasy), Robin uses hypertech like a Virtual Adpet, Lord Fanny uses either a Dreamspeaker tradition or a Mesoamerican Craft. Boy is the only one who doesn't use overt magic that I can recall (at least not with the support of the others), but her use of martial arts may qualify as Do, and her magic is just super subtle. Jack is an Orphan, and the enemies are a cross between Nephandi and Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T20:25:23-08:00","id":810941,"title":"","content":"The vampires from What we do in Shadows , vladysvlad, petyr, The Beast, deacon , viago, Nick and Stu. Their clans and The tribes of The werewolfs and The Camera Crew","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:28:46-08:00","id":822543,"title":"","content":"Ok, explain The game Persona 3 in WoD terms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T08:51:46-08:00","id":824953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=822543#post822543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, explain The game Persona 3 in WoD terms</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm still playing through it, but I'll try to do the basics, at least.<br /> <br /> Mage is once again the default explanation - when the characters are fighting monsters, they do so in an Umbral realm where Paradox from their spells is minimized, and they all have manifested Avatars that they summon through their Focus (they're all also part of their own Craft/Tradition, though which one is up in the air still - a Spirit-focused Son of Ether or Virtual Adept works, but they could also be Technocrats). Each one focuses on different spheres according to their personal element (and their Persona's/Avatar's Essence and Resonance).<br /> <br /> However, it's not the only explanation. Another possibility is that they are Eastern Changelings, possessed as children with the Elemental variant, and their Personas are the manifestation of their Changeling Soul. Alternatively, they could also be Demons, but (at least with the main character) whose demon selves have amnesia about what they truly are; they see their Demonic forms and Lores as &quot;summoning their Persona.&quot; Finally, they could be Gnosis-bearing Kinfolk who all have personal totems, or Bastet with Jamak who simply don't shift into battle forms (possibly because they don't know how yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T12:13:11-08:00","id":844090,"title":"","content":"Prepare for Trash here is what the Undertale cast would be as WOD creatures <b>SPOILERS BELOW</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Frisk: Mage: Virtual Adept/Nephandi in Genocide run<br /> Toriel: Changling:Pooka<br /> Papyrus:Wraith: Risen Wraith<br /> Sans: Wraith: Risen Wraith:Papyru's Shadow<br /> Undyne: Changling: One of the Kith from Blood Dimmed Tides<br /> Alphys: Changling: A Nocker that looks like a lizard?<br /> Mettaton: Either a Wraith or an <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Inanimae from Changling <br /> Asgore: Changling:Pooka</span></span><br /> Flowey/Asriel; An awakened construct?<br /> Chara: Frisk's Avatar<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T01:47:49-08:00","id":844978,"title":"","content":"Wow, it's funny when you look back at much older posts that you make in this thread. Since I have a really hard time fitting Hunter with Gravity Falls now since the show finally concluded.<br /> I'll stick to the list of characters that fall under the Zodiac so far then:<br /> <br /> <b>Fiddleford McGucket: </b>Dauntain, former Seelie Nocker.<br /> This one is so obvious once you get to the Society of the Blind Eye episode. Not only is McGucket excellent at building absurd machines a Nocker would love, but... <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">McGucket saw something that made him unable to cope with a fae-like reality and builds a device to help him forget it. Then he tries to help other people to forget what they saw. He, however, eventually slowly gets over his Dauntain status with the help from Dipper and Mabel.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Stanford Pines: </b>Son of Ether Mage who was once very close to becoming a Marauder.<br /> Ford is certainly the sort of &quot;SCIENCE!&quot; or mad scientist type of character, which is why I went with the Son of Ether choice. But he was also close to being a Order of Hermes Mage as well.<br /> His brush with Marauder-ism was due to Bill getting him into such a paranoid state. Ford was lost in the Umbra and couldn't get back for some time. And Ford's Journals are certainly strong Mage Wonders. Stanford also &quot;Awakened&quot; first, so he cannot become a Garou like his brother, Stanley, did.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Stan Pines: </b>Ronin Garou, Homid, ex-Silent Strider. Also had the Rite of Renunciation performed on him. Stan has also dealt with Harano at certain times in his life.<br /> <b>Soos: </b>Mortal with Numina powers.Soos can often eerily predict things before they happen at times.<br /> <b>Wendy: </b>Fianna Ahroun Homid Lost Cub or Fianna Kinfolk.Wendy hasn't experienced the change just yet.<br /> <b>Robbie V.: </b>Risen... just kidding! That was a reference to a popular theory that went around in the early days of the show's fandom, though. Mortal with certain Numina powers dealing with the dead. Robbie probably has familiarity with wraiths, though, considering the work his parents do. Maybe, there's a chance he will become a Euthanatoi or Hollow One Mage?<br /> <b>Pacfica: </b>I wonder if her family has any connection to a Mummy with the karchakka flaw... 'get it'? Otherwise, Pacifica is just a normal very rich mortal with strong connections/influence.<br /> <b>Gideon: </b>Very young Sorcerer or Hedge Wizard.<br /> <b>Dipper Pines: </b>Because of the connection to two characters (<i>See spoilers in this post if you have watched the show til the end</i>), Dipper has the chance of either &quot;awakening&quot; or going through the first change. If he &quot;awakens&quot; first: Order of Hermes Mage, pretty much. If he experiences the &quot;Change&quot; first: Silent Strider Galliard. There's also the chance he won't become either as well.<br /> <b>Mabel Pines: </b>Because of the connection to two characters (<i>See spoilers in this post if you have watched the show til the end</i>), Mabel has the chance of either &quot;awakening&quot; or going through the first change. If she &quot;awakens&quot; first: Cult of Ecstasy Mage. If she experiences the &quot;Change&quot; first: Silent Strider Galliard. There's also the chance she won't become either as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Bill: </b>A really nasty aspect of the Wyld or a very strong Wyld Incarna that isn't your friend... and will resort to underhanded tactics to get what he wants. Bill's goal is to unleash the Wyld's power unto the whole world to have his 'fun' and to break the barrier between reality and the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 03-10-2016, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:08:35-07:00","id":913614,"title":"","content":"Not sure if anyone ever answered these, but since I've been on such a big DC Comics tip with Rebirth...<br /> <br /> <br /> Nightwing?<br /> Green Lantern?<br /> Red Lanterns(Atrocitus and Bleez)?<br /> Cyborg?<br /> Wonder Woman?<br /> The Flash?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></s