path.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T20:12:05-07:00","id":935908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=934468#post934468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always seen the Lost Boys as Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of the Lost Boys as Sabbat Tzimisce because of the modifications to the toes that let them hang upside down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:08:07-07:00","id":941631,"title":"","content":"Elric of Melnibon\u00e9 and jeremiah cornelius :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:01:16-07:00","id":943549,"title":"","content":"Elric (as Elric, not as the Eternal Champion) seems to be a Dark Ages style Mage with a terrible Wonder for a sword. His magic is far too vulgar to be a modern mage, but he's also not strictly anything else. Realistically, his character fits more as an Abyssal Exalt, but for WoD, I'd put him as an Archaic Mage with a unique set of Pillars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:09:38-07:00","id":943726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/42557-which-creature-group-would-blank-fictional-character-would-be-in?p=933068#post933068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also see the Lost Boys as Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are. Towns do not become &quot;Murder Capitals&quot; when Anarchs are there. Anarchs are not so kill-happy. You know who does that? The Sabbat.<br /> <br /> They also drink blood from one bottle. You know who does that? The Sabbat.<br /> <br /> They also like celebrating around a big bonfire. You know who does that? Yes, you know.<br /> <br /> They are also a seemingly wild and free pack that actually serves an old, smart, powerful hidden &quot;vampire in charge&quot;. You know who is organized like that? Yes.<br /> <br /> Also explains their feet: a friendly Tzimisce did this for them. As for their clan... they are Brujah Antitribu. Except some one of them who is Ravnos Antitrubu: he did the maggot prank.<br /> <br /> The vampires from Near Dark, on the other hand, are pretty much Gangrel Antitribu to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","user":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","name":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:04:40-07:00","id":943760,"title":"","content":"Of course, the entire group in Lost Boys could be Panders, as they do not seem to have a real organization. The master vampire could be an 8th generation Pander (probably raised through diabolorie) who is trying to create a sick Sabbat family in the city. The Chimestry and Vicissitude could just be odd manifestations of the way that Panders develop Disciplines. They seem to be able to fly though, which would suggest the third level of Movement of the Mind, which would also suggest that the master vampire looted some Thaumaturgical knowledge from Tremere Antitribu (or found some other source of Blood Magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":